  <!-- SECTION 2: ASSEMBLY DETAILS & STATUS -->
  <section id="assembly-details" aria-labelledby="assembly-details-heading">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="assembly-details-heading">Assembly Details &amp; Status</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-panel">
    <div class="assembly-cards-grid">
      <!-- V5 Card -->
      <article class="assembly-detail-card is-current-card">
        <div class="assembly-detail-header">
          <div>
            <h3 class="assembly-detail-title">Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0 <span class="assembly-detail-version">\(v5\)</span></h3>
            <span class="assembly-detail-sub">Current Gold-Standard Representative Reference</span>
          </div>
          <span class="assembly-badge assembly-badge-active">Active Standard</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assembly-detail-metrics">
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">2,182 Mb</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Total Assembled</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">47.0 Mb</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Contig N50</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">10</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Pseudomolecules</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">675</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Unplaced Scaffolds</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="assembly-detail-desc">De novo assembly constructed from PacBio Sequel long-read sequencing technology. Scaffolds validated and anchored by BioNano optical mapping and genetic linkage maps. Annotated with <code>Zm00001eb.1</code> containing sequentially numbered gene models.</p>
        <div class="assembly-detail-links">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="/genome/assembly/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0">Assembly Profile</a>
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0/">Download Directory</a>
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/bioproject/PRJEB32225" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NCBI BioProject</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- V4 Card -->
      <article class="assembly-detail-card">
        <div class="assembly-detail-header">
          <div>
            <h3 class="assembly-detail-title">Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0 <span class="assembly-detail-version">\(v4\)</span></h3>
            <span class="assembly-detail-sub">PacBio Single-Molecule Real-Time Assembly</span>
          </div>
          <span class="assembly-badge">v4 Reference</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assembly-detail-metrics">
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">2,134 Mb</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Total Assembled</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">1.28 Mb</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Contig N50</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">10</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Pseudomolecules</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">256</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Unplaced Scaffolds</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="assembly-detail-desc">Complete de novo assembly generated using PacBio single-molecule technology on high-molecular-weight DNA extracted from a descendant of the accession used for v1&ndash;v3 assemblies \(PI 677128\). Annotated with Filtered Gene Set <code>Zm00001d.2</code>.</p>
        <div class="assembly-detail-links">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="/genome/assembly/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0">Assembly Profile</a>
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0/">Download Directory</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- V3 Card -->
      <article class="assembly-detail-card">
        <div class="assembly-detail-header">
          <div>
            <h3 class="assembly-detail-title">B73 RefGen_v3 <span class="assembly-detail-version">\(v3\)</span></h3>
            <span class="assembly-detail-sub">BAC Framework with WGS Gap Closure</span>
          </div>
          <span class="assembly-badge">v3 Legacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assembly-detail-metrics">
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">2,068 Mb</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Total Assembled</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">10</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Pseudomolecules</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">213</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">New Gene Models</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">251</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Improved Models</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="assembly-detail-desc">Captured missing gene space in v2 using whole-genome shotgun \(WGS\) sequence reads. Introduced 213 new gene models, improved 251 gene models, and merged 10 models. Annotated with <code>5b+</code> and MAKER-P gene sets.</p>
        <div class="assembly-detail-links">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="/genome/assembly/B73%20RefGen_v3">Assembly Profile</a>
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="https://download.maizegdb.org/B73_RefGen_v3/">Download Directory</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- V2 & V1 Card -->
      <article class="assembly-detail-card">
        <div class="assembly-detail-header">
          <div>
            <h3 class="assembly-detail-title">B73 RefGen_v2 &amp; RefGen_v1</h3>
            <span class="assembly-detail-sub">Foundational BAC Physical Map Assemblies</span>
          </div>
          <span class="assembly-badge">Historic BAC</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assembly-detail-metrics">
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">2,061 Mb</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">v1 Assembly</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">2,066 Mb</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">v2 Assembly</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">10</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Chromosomes</span></div>
          <div class="assembly-metric-item"><span class="assembly-metric-value">2009</span><span class="assembly-metric-label">Initial Release</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="assembly-detail-desc">RefGen_v1 was the first complete sequencing of the maize B73 genome using BAC-by-BAC Sanger sequencing \(Schnable et al. 2009\). RefGen_v2 improved the ordering and orientation of intra-BAC contigs using the minimum tiling path \(MTP\).</p>
        <div class="assembly-detail-links">
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="/genome/assembly/B73%20RefGen_v2">RefGen_v2 Profile</a>
          <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary mgdb-button-sm" href="/genome/assembly/B73%20RefGen_v1">RefGen_v1 Profile</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  
    </div>

    <!-- Five releases, one unit per axis: how long the pieces are, how many
         there are, and how much of the conserved gene space is present. Every
         value is measured from the distributed files -- the same scan behind
         the Genome Data Hub -- so the figures cannot drift from /genome. -->
    <div class="mgdb-chart-grid assembly-charts" data-series="$(assembly_series)">
      <figure class="mgdb-figure assembly-chart-wide">
        <h3>How long the pieces are</h3>
        <div class="mgdb-chart" id="assembly-contiguity-chart" role="img"
             aria-label="Logarithmic line chart of contig N50, largest contig and scaffold N50 across the five B73 reference assemblies, 2009 to 2020">
          <span class="mgdb-chart-fallback">Loading assembly contiguity&hellip;</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Contig N50 rose from 39.9 kb in v1 to 47.0 Mb in v5, a factor of 1,178, while scaffold N50 held near 220 Mb throughout. The gain is entirely inside the chromosomes&#58; every release has been chromosome-scale, so what long reads bought was continuous sequence rather than a better chromosome model. Logarithmic axis.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="mgdb-figure">
        <h3>How many pieces there are</h3>
        <div class="mgdb-chart" id="assembly-fragments-chart" role="img"
             aria-label="Logarithmic line chart of the number of contigs and the number of gaps in the five B73 reference assemblies">
          <span class="mgdb-chart-fallback">Loading fragment counts&hellip;</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>The three BAC-era assemblies were each built from about 125,000 contigs separated by about as many gaps. v5 has 1,393 contigs and 708 gaps. Logarithmic axis.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="mgdb-figure">
        <h3>How complete the gene space is</h3>
        <div class="mgdb-chart" id="assembly-completeness-chart" role="img"
             aria-label="Line chart of genome and protein single-copy ortholog completeness for the five B73 reference assemblies">
          <span class="mgdb-chart-fallback">Loading completeness&hellip;</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Conserved single-copy orthologs recovered from the assembly itself and from the proteins of its annotation. The sequence was already 95.4% complete in 2009, so this is the axis with the least room to move; the annotation is what took until v4 to catch up.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    $(assembly_stats_table)

    <p class="mgdb-note">Measured by MaizeGDB from the distributed FASTA and GFF3 files rather than copied from the publications, so these are the numbers for the files this page links to. Completeness is compleasm 0.2.9 &#40;genome&#41; and BUSCO 5.8.3 &#40;proteins&#41;, both against poales_odb10.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3: GENE MODELS & NOMENCLATURE -->
  <section id="assembly-nomenclature" aria-labelledby="assembly-nomenclature-heading">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="assembly-nomenclature-heading">B73 Reference Gene Models &amp; Nomenclature Standards</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-panel">
    <div class="assembly-notice-box">
      <strong>Important Annotation Notice&#58;</strong>
      <p>The B73 v5 and NAM founders genome assemblies were initially released with a preliminary annotation \(<code>Zm00001e.1</code>\). The official annotation \(<code>Zm00001eb.1</code>\) features refined gene models and sequentially numbered identifiers across chromosomes. Use the official <code>Zm00001eb.1</code> gene models for current analyses. Cross-references between preliminary, v4, and v3 models are available below.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-table-scroll">
      <table class="mgdb-table">
