  <!-- SECTION 6: STOCK & ORIGIN -->
  <section id="assembly-stocks" aria-labelledby="assembly-stocks-heading">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="assembly-stocks-heading">B73 Stock Information &amp; Pedigree Origin</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-panel">
    <div class="assembly-stock-content">
      <p>The seed source for both <strong>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0</strong> and <strong>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0</strong> descended from <a class="mgdb-link" href="https://npgsweb.ars-grin.gov/gringlobal/accessiondetail.aspx?accid=PI+550473" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PI 550473</a>, maintained at the North Central Regional Plant Introduction Station \(NCRPIS\). The accession closest to the seed lot used for sequencing was deposited as <a class="mgdb-link" href="https://npgsweb.ars-grin.gov/gringlobal/accessiondetail.aspx?accid=PI+677128" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PI 677128</a>.</p>
      
      <p>The B73 source for the original BAC libraries \(BACs with prefix <code>b</code> constructed in Rod Wing's lab; BACs with prefix <code>c</code> constructed in Peter deJong's lab\) was derived from the Coe PI 550473 line. High-Molecular-Weight DNA was prepared by Jack Gardiner at the University of Missouri.</p>
      
      <p>Specific details regarding pedigree validation, contig frameworks, and physical maps are described in <a class="mgdb-link" href="/reference/9017907">Coe &amp; Schaeffer \(2005\) <i>Maydica</i> 50&#58;285-303</a> [<a class="mgdb-link" href="/docs/B73materials.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PDF</a>].</p>
    </div>
  
    </div>
  </section>

