  <!-- SECTION: FAQS
       The card grid the project pages use \(/NAM_project#nam-faqs\), not a
       <details> accordion: six short answers are cheaper to scan open than to
       open one at a time, and this is the shape the group settled on there. -->
  <section id="assembly-faqs" aria-labelledby="assembly-faqs-heading">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="assembly-faqs-heading">FAQs</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-card-grid assembly-faqs-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>What is a representative reference genome?</h3>
        <p>A reference genome is a haploid representation of a species' DNA sequence with a defined coordinate system, version identifier, and structural annotations. B73 is the representative reference genome for <i>Zea mays</i>, and is the common coordinate system for genetic maps, variant catalogs, and pan-genome comparisons.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>What changed between RefGen_v4 and Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0?</h3>
        <p>v5 is a de novo assembly from PacBio Sequel long reads, validated against BioNano optical maps. Contig N50 rose from 1.28 Mb in v4 to 47.0 Mb, the number of contigs fell from 2,786 to 1,393, and the number of gaps fell from 2,520 to 708. The figures in Details plot the five releases against each other.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>Why was a preliminary v5 annotation released, and which set should I use?</h3>
        <p>A preliminary annotation \(<code>Zm00001e.1</code>\) was released alongside the initial v5 assembly to give early access. It was superseded by the official annotation, <code>Zm00001eb.1</code>, which has refined gene boundaries and gene models numbered in sequential order along each chromosome. Use <code>Zm00001eb.1</code>.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>How do I translate coordinates between assembly versions?</h3>
        <p>Chain files between v4 and v5 are in the <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0/chain_files/">v5 chain files directory</a> and work with LiftOver or CrossMap. For v2 to v3, use the <a href="http://ensembl.gramene.org/tools.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ensembl assembly converter</a>.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>How do I identify the Filtered Gene Set in RefGen_v3?</h3>
        <p>In the <code>5b+</code> gene build, the models that were the Filtered Gene Set are classified as protein-coding models in the GFF3 and FASTA files.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>Where are the legacy resources from MaizeSequence.org?</h3>
        <p>Historical files, gene builds and FTP dumps from MaizeSequence.org are held in the <a href="ftp://ftp.gramene.org/pub/gramene/maizesequence.org/">Gramene MaizeSequence FTP archive</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

